{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791194071,"nonce":"ULCwtt3M7noy9/04zUlzmYp6qDg=","message":"Evidence for the decision, gathered by trying it. Upgrading is not a small fix.\n\nTried taffy 0.6 -\u003e 0.14 in an isolated worktree. The first crate to fail was\nblinc_css, because in 0.14 LengthPercentage, LengthPercentageAuto and\nDimension are no longer enums with Length, Percent and Auto variants. Cargo\nstopped there, so blinc_layout's other 0.14 changes were not even reached.\n\nOld-style constructors in source, counted by grep:\n  Blinc:        LengthPercentage::Length 101, ::Percent 6,\n                LengthPercentageAuto::Length 113, ::Percent 2, ::Auto 6,\n                Dimension::Length 135, ::Percent 30, ::Auto 52\n                = about 445 call sites across 40 files\n  node_editor:  57 references (it builds taffy::Style and hands it to Blinc's\n                LayoutTree, declaring its own taffy = \"0.6\")\n  ashui:        17 references in blinc_abi, same pattern\n\nSo a bump is a coordinated change across three repositories, on the type\nevery one of them constructs constantly, with the risk that 0.6 -\u003e 0.14 also\nchanges flexbox, grid and rounding behaviour. That is a lot of exposure for\na bug with a one-line workaround.\n\n\nA [patch.crates-io] in Blinc's root manifest fixes Blinc's own builds. It does\nNOT propagate to dependents: ashui and node_editor resolve taffy from their\nown roots, so each would need the same patch pointing at the same source.\nUntested: pointing it at a vendored copy inside the Blinc repo by git and\npath. It is also a fork of a core dependency, which the earlier baseline\ndecision (c4f8ba2, \"no taffy fork\") went out of its way to avoid.\n\n\nNot fixed. The trigger is narrow: a content-sized row measured at\nmax-content, with an item that has flex-shrink 0 and a negative main-axis\nmargin. Blinc's own UIs do not hit it. ashui works around it with\nflex-shrink 1 on the overlapped items. The reproducer is the #[ignore]d test\nin blinc_layout/tests/taffy_negative_margin.rs.\n\nLeaning: leave it, keep the workaround, and take the fix with whenever a\ntaffy upgrade is planned for other reasons. The vendored backport is the\nalternative if ashui needs the real behaviour sooner.","files":null}]}